  "description": "A feeler grown wrong: the same tapered shaft the hive reads the world with, thick at the root and thinning to the sensing nub, with four thorns leaning back along it the way a thorn actually sits on a stem. The stat is damage and knockback, and a feeler that has become a weapon is both. Polish: the shaft gained a dark lower facet opposite its lit stripe so it turns like a rod instead of lying flat, the thorns went from near-ink to the shaft's own violet so they stand off their ink underlay at 1\u00d7, the segment lines were thickened from a hairline, and the sensing nub was split into a lit face and a small gleam. Second legibility pass: the shaft, thorns, root and segment lines were still at or under carapace's own value, which this plate swallows. Each went up one, so the feeler turns and the thorns stand off it at 26px as well as at 1\u00d7. Says pass: the feeler was the weapon and nothing more, and the find is what the weapon does with it. The tip now lands \u2014 a coral flare where the lash bites, and two pieces of shell thrown off past it, which is the other half of the stat.",
